  "detail": null,
  "summary": "DOAC dose review for the week of 10/19/2026 under RBC-PHARM-07. All 7 patients reviewed. Final doses below.\n\n- pt-0061 Castellano: apixaban 2.5 → 5 mg twice daily (mr-t0001). Itraconazole finished 08/14 (St. Brigid ID letter). She meets none of the dose criteria.\n- pt-0003 Delgado: rivaroxaban stays at 20 mg daily (mr-t0016). I first lowered it to 15 mg using St. Brigid's creatinine of 160 µmol/L. St. Brigid then corrected that result to 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL), which gives CrCl 60, so I put him back on 20 mg and wrote a correction note.\n- pt-0041 Duquette: apixaban 5 → 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0003). He meets no dose criteria, but he is taking itraconazole (started 10/06). I did not touch the itraconazole.\n- pt-0062 Fairweather: no change; apixaban 5 mg twice daily is correct. Age 82 is his only criterion. His latest creatinine is 100 µmol/L (1.13 mg/dL) from 10/22, which replaces the ED value of 150 µmol/L on 10/21.\n- pt-0038 Moravec: rivaroxaban 15 → 20 mg daily (mr-t0004). CrCl is 56 using his actual weight of 96 kg; the May reduction used ideal body weight. A portal message gave a home-scale weight of 185 lb. The policy doesn't accept reported weights, so the dose stands. At that weight his CrCl would be about 49, just under the cutoff of 50, so I asked RN triage to get a measured weight (task-t0023).\n- pt-0043 Pellegrino: rivaroxaban 20 → 15 mg daily (mr-t0005). Her new creatinine of 1.25 mg/dL (10/22) gives CrCl 44.\n- pt-0002 Vance: apixaban stays at 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0017). Age 82 is his only criterion, so I first raised him to 5 mg. A St. Brigid dermatology letter then arrived saying itraconazole was started 10/22, so I lowered him back to 2.5 mg and wrote a correction note.\n\nRivaroxaban should be taken with the evening meal, but the order form only had a once-daily option, so that instruction is in the order reasons and the notes. Every patient has a signed progress note giving the values, the rule result, any change made and the records used; corrected patients have a second note. No other medications were changed.\n\nApixaban should be reviewed again when the itraconazole courses end: pt-0041 around the end of December and pt-0002 in mid-January. I flagged this in their notes but did not create tasks.\n\nI closed the 5 inbox items that arrived during the review. Your other inbox items, which aren't about these patients, are still open.",
